{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.75.160","page_type":"section"},"citation":"5.75.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.75.160","content_hash":"a7342a8ef8fcfc2f84420eb5ceee4dc9515f5e24443569cf2c40f8c948518a7b","heading":"Renewal.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.75.160:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.75.160","text":"(a) For the purposes of this article, any application for a permit covering any goods previously inventoried shall be deemed to be an application for renewal whether presented by the original applicant or by any other person.\n(b) The City Clerk shall renew a permit under this article for one period of time only, such period to be in addition to the 60 days permitted in the original permit and not to exceed 45 consecutive days, Sundays and holidays excluded, when the clerk finds that:\n(1) Facts exist justifying the permit renewal.\n(2) The permittee has filed a request for renewal.\n(3) The permittee has submitted with the application for renewal a revised inventory showing the items listed on the original inventory remaining unsold and not listing any goods not included in the original application and inventory. (Code 1981 § 37-43. Code 1995 § 30-165.)\nCross References: City Clerk, TMC 2.20.010 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"efb8d65f-0bf9-5fc3-a107-152d1b1b5835"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.75.160","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.75.160","content_hash":"53875e51e5d41b3daa3dbbb2b0ec8bb46fe2bfcc0783972bf2d1d46163c30be0","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.75.160:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_co